      },
      "text": "Clinical psychology sits at the intersection of science and practice. Diagnostic\nsystems (DSM-5, ICD-11) provide a common vocabulary that is largely atheoretical\nand category-based — which is convenient for clinical communication but increasingly\ndisconnected from neuroscience and dimensional reality. Evidence-based treatments exist\nfor most major disorders, with CBT having the broadest support."
